                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is one of those \"what do I say about it?\" sort of games, if interactive fiction can be called a game. In the nuts and bolts, you have a delightfully-nostalgic amber-screen monitor aesthetic going (back to the good 'ol 80s) coupled with an outstanding atmospheric soundtrack. But it's the details where you find the worth of this one.\n\nBasically, you're on a flight to a star about 20 light years away from Earth. Like all mid-hop flights these days, there are few amenities - no food, no in flight entertainment, no cabin crew even - but there is free wi-fi and social networks still live, so there's a way to kill time. But since you're covering 20 LY in about 30 minutes, there's a price to pay: time dilation. Thirty minutes for you, decades for everybody not on the ship. Including your friends online. \n\nIt's a story of a third of a life, experienced by your friends, but told with a strobe light: you only get momentary glimpses, each separated from the next by years, not hours or days. And yet, since it's social media, you're going to interact with it. Who cares if your responses are a year out of date? You're participating!\n\nKTLS as I'm going to call this game is...well, it's different, and it's a lot of things. Exactly what is up to your interpretation. Social commentary? Sure, and lots of it. Indictment of an increasingly tech-obsessed but ethically-bankrupt society? Maybe. A demonstration in a handful of minutes of the impermanence of friendships, the mercurial nature of human interaction? Probably. Depressing? Altogether likely, but not certain.\n\nLook, this is a piece of art, literary art. Maybe not high art, but as art it's open to interpretation, and everybody is going to get something a little bit different out of it. You'll have to draw your own conclusions and lessons from it, because it's going to get into your head a little differently than mine, and that's a good thing; it's what makes us human. \n\n(If you're looking for a TLDR, here you go: the fact that you're looking for one says that this game isn't for you. Lots of *gaspshockhorror* reading here.)",
